      "message": "Could we skip IPsec cleanup for child SAs that have not been installed yet? An initiator awaiting IKE_AUTH matches this callback, but its child\u0027s local_sa_id and remote_sa_id are still zero. Deleting it calls ikev2_del_tunnel_from_main(), which unlocks unrelated SA IDs 0 and 2048.\n\nI reproduced this under debug ASAN: configure an independent IPsec SA with ID 0, complete IKE_SA_INIT without replying to IKE_AUTH, then delete the profile\u0027s tunnel interface. The unrelated SA disappears. Please also cover this handshake window in the regression test.",
